8	//! Run-scoped callback-independent process publication and recipient permits.
9	//!
10	//! Installation precedes guest startup. A permit authorizes one actual task
11	//! continuation, not a host wake or an unrelated borrowed Guest. Generation-
12	//! bound child completion is published through this same run-scoped control.
13	//!
14	//! Active publication uses only transaction -> lifecycle -> run failure ->
15	//! process signals and pinned private eventfd carriers. It never acquires or
16	//! pins the ordinary file table. The retained inactive alarm test endpoint
17	//! additionally takes file table first, preserving its negative controls.
18	//! Image validation briefly reacquires image below transaction;
19	//! child lookup briefly reacquires registry below lifecycle. Those guards are
20	//! released before failure/process acquisition. The run failure guard remains
21	//! held through readiness I/O after process/lifecycle guards are released,
22	//! serializing publications across
23	//! processes in this run. Existing executor process/thread locks remain below
24	//! the transaction. No registry or retirement mutex is held during host closes.
